#
# What the fluid-runner image installs. requirements.txt is compiled from this
# file with every distribution pinned by version and sha256, for every
# platform:
#   ./compile.sh
# These versions must match versions.lock.yaml (built_images, fluid-runner
# `contents`); tests/launcher/test_build.py checks that.
#
# forge is built from the source archive of one commit of Agenticstiger/forge-cli
# (the archive is checked against the lock's sha256 by the Dockerfile), so it is
# not in requirements.txt: compile.sh reads only its dependencies from here, and
# --no-emit-package keeps forge itself out. The commit below is the lock's.
data-product-forge[local,aws] @ https://github.com/Agenticstiger/forge-cli/archive/c826f3ae698493dd43aaa00a1dc63bafb29dba52.tar.gz
dbt-core==1.10.23
dbt-trino==1.10.6
duckdb==1.5.6
